# PSR-7b — Secret-scan baseline (tracked files)

## Intent

Close PSR-7 **R-SECRET** tooling gap for **tracked files only**:

- Pure-Node scanner over `git ls-files` (no new root package dependency)
- Machine-readable allowlist for known fixtures / `.example` placeholders
- Optional `.gitleaks.toml` stub for later binary-backed CI (not required to pass)
- **No** git-history scan claim
- **No** required CI workflow / branch-protection change
- **No** full gate

## Scanner

```bash
node scripts/ops/secret-scan-tracked-baseline.mjs
# ratchet:
node scripts/ops/psr-7b-secret-scan-baseline-smoke.mjs
```

Families: `private_key` (placeholder PEM filtered), `aws_access_key`,
`github_pat`, `slack_token`, `stripe_live_key`.

Exit codes:

| Code | Meaning |
| ---: | --- |
| 0 | No unallowlisted high-confidence hits |
| 1 | Unallowlisted hit(s) or ratchet drift |
| 2 | Scanner infrastructure error |

## Baseline result (tip scan)

| Metric | Value |
| --- | ---: |
| Open hits | 0 |
| Allowlisted | 1 (`legacy/apps/api/test/e2e/jwt-test-keys.ts`) |

Connection-string / env-assignment entropy sweeps are **deferred** — local CI
intentionally uses `app_tour:app_tour` fixtures that drown high-signal rules.

## Scope honesty

| In scope | Out of scope (needs YES / later slice) |
| --- | --- |
| Tracked blob content at tip | Full git history (`gitleaks detect`) |
| High-confidence token/PEM families | Connection-string entropy sweeps |
| Allowlist YAML + `.gitleaks.toml` stub | Required check on `main` |
| Document open findings | Auto-remediation of legacy env files |

## Open findings policy

Baseline may record **known debt** (e.g. tracked `legacy/**/.env.development`)
as inventory rows with `status: open_debt` without failing the smoke if those
paths are explicitly allowlisted with rationale. New unallowlisted hits fail.

